From: WinTone01 <mertbayinma792@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:01:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Slow client protection

Disconnect connections whose outbound backlog exceeds a limit
(shulker.yml network.slow-client-protection). A client that stops
reading is dropped by the keep-alive timeout after 30 s, but until then
the server keeps encoding packets for it into direct memory; with many
such connections it runs out (OutOfDirectMemoryError), affecting every
player.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
index 9fbc7e93712672dbab67f931e2aee447d803607b..7819f387474bbd706b97e74f14e1413601c9947e 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
@@ -595,6 +595,7 @@ public class Connection extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<Packet<?>> {
     private static int joinAttemptsThisTick; // Paper - Buffer joins to world
     private static int currTick; // Paper - Buffer joins to world
     public void tick() {
+        dev.shulker.server.network.SlowClientGuard.check(this, this.channel); // Shulker - slow client protection
         this.flushQueue();
         // Paper start - Buffer joins to world
         if (Connection.currTick != net.minecraft.server.MinecraftServer.currentTick) {
